s5-2-p13 = prose (cons "The distinction generalizes to language translation. A parser maps a text representation to syntax and may reject malformed text. An elaborator maps surface syntax and a context to a typed term, perhaps with implicit arguments resolved. An interpreter maps a term to a semantic construction. A compiler maps one representation to another with an explicit behavioral relation. Each map is a function or relation that can itself be defined, evaluated, transformed, and proved about. **There is no universal necessity that these maps be composed in a fixed order.**" nil)
